    "Description": "This is a kernel live patch module which can be loaded by the kpatch command line utility to modify the code of a running kernel.  This patch module is targeted for kernel-5.14.0-427.68.2.el9_4.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* kernel: ipv6: icmp: clear skb2-\u003ecb[] in ip6_err_gen_icmpv6_unreach() (CVE-2026-43038)\n\n* kernel: dlm: validate length in dlm_search_rsb_tree (CVE-2026-43125)\n\n* kernel: netfilter: flowtable: strictly check for maximum number of actions (CVE-2026-43329)\n\n* kernel: net: sched: UAF via missing handler for TC_ACT_CONSUMED in tcf_qevent_handle (CVE-2026-64530)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
